%N A399118 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n, k) is the number of inclusion-maximal Sidon subsets of {1, ..., n} having cardinality k, where A382397(n) <= k <= A143824(n).
%C A399118 A Sidon subset is a subset for which all positive differences between distinct elements are different; equivalently, all unordered sums of two not necessarily distinct elements are different.
%C A399118 "Inclusion-maximal" means that no further element of {1, ..., n} can be adjoined while preserving the Sidon property. This is different from having maximum possible cardinality.
%C A399118 The row indexed by n contains the cardinality distribution of all maximal Sidon subsets counted by A325879(n).
%C A399118 The lower row bound A382397(n) is the minimum cardinality of a maximal Sidon subset of {1, ..., n}. The upper row bound A143824(n) is the maximum cardinality of a Sidon subset of {1, ..., n}; every maximum-cardinality Sidon subset is inclusion-maximal.
%C A399118 The support {k : T(n, k) > 0} is the saturated Sidon cardinality spectrum of {1, ..., n}. For 1 <= n <= 183 this support has been verified to be an interval of consecutive integers.
%C A399118 The linked preprint proves that an inclusion-maximal Sidon subset of cardinality 8 exists for n = 144, whereas none exists for n >= 145.
%H A399118 Felix Huber, <a href="/A399118/a399118.txt">Maple program</a>.
%H A399118 Felix Huber, <a href="/A399118/a399118.pdf">Saturated Sidon Sets in Consecutive Intervals: The Eight-Mark Threshold Is 144</a>, preprint, 2026.
%F A399118 Sum_{k = A382397(n) .. A143824(n)} T(n, k) = A325879(n).
%F A399118 T(n, A143824(n)) = A382395(n).
%F A399118 min{k : T(n, k) > 0} = A382397(n).
%F A399118 max{k : T(n, k) > 0} = A143824(n).
