%e A399118 For n = 4, A382397(4) = 2 and A143824(4) = 3, so the row consists of the entries T(4, 2) and T(4, 3). The unique inclusion-maximal Sidon subset of cardinality 2 is {2, 3}: adjoining 1 gives {1, 2, 3}, which has the repeated difference 1, and adjoining 4 gives {2, 3, 4}, which again has the repeated difference 1. The two inclusion-maximal Sidon subsets of cardinality 3 are {1, 2, 4} and {1, 3, 4}. Hence row 4 is 1, 2.
